<section class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs" aria-labelledby="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs-heading">
  <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__container">
    <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__header">
      <span class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__eyebrow">FAQs</span>
      <h2 id="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs-heading" class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <p class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__sub">Everything else people ask when picking between Formester and Qualtrics.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__list">
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__q">Why do teams switch away from Qualtrics?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__a">Three reasons dominate on Reddit and G2 reviews: transparent pricing (Qualtrics is enterprise-quoted, so teams can't budget without a sales call), speed to first form (Qualtrics onboarding often takes weeks with a mandatory sales demo), and per-user cost (Qualtrics charges per user, which balloons as teams grow). Formester's free plan is unlimited and self-serve, and paid tiers cap at $49/month for 25 team seats.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__q">Is Formester really a Qualtrics replacement?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__a">For most survey and form use cases, yes. Formester ships an AI form generator, quiz auto-scoring, drop-off analytics, custom email notifications, and native payment collection on the free plan. The genuine gaps: SOC 2 / ISO 27001 / HIPAA / FedRAMP certifications (which Qualtrics has), and specialized research tooling like IRB workflows and panel management (which Qualtrics's ResearchXM does).</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__q">Is there a free Qualtrics alternative?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__a">Yes. Formester's free plan gives you unlimited forms, unlimited responses, AI form generator, quiz auto-scoring, drop-off analytics, and payment collection at $0/month with no per-user seat charge. Qualtrics's free account allows 3 active surveys with up to 30 questions each and 500 responses, which works for evaluation but not for production volume.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__q">What about open-source Qualtrics alternatives like LimeSurvey?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__a">LimeSurvey is a legitimate open-source option if you have devops capacity to self-host and don't need modern form UX. Formester is hosted (nothing to install), ships an AI generator, native payments, and a modern editor that LimeSurvey doesn't match. Choose LimeSurvey if data sovereignty is non-negotiable; choose Formester if you want a working product day one.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__q">Which is better for students or academic research?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__a">For a simple class project or student survey, Formester's free plan (unlimited responses) outgrows Qualtrics's free tier (500 responses, 3 active surveys) the moment a survey takes off. For thesis-level academic research that needs IRB approval and panel recruitment, Qualtrics ResearchXM remains the specialized tool of choice.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__q">Can I export my Qualtrics surveys and responses into Formester?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__a">Yes. Export responses as CSV or SPSS from the Data &amp; Analysis tab, and export the survey structure as a QSF file. In Formester, either paste the question list into the AI generator or rebuild in the drag-and-drop builder. Most single-survey migrations finish in 20-30 minutes.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__q">When is Qualtrics still the better choice?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__a">Regulated research (healthcare, government, financial services) that requires SOC 2, HIPAA, or FedRAMP. Large panel-based studies with IRB workflows. Enterprise CX programs with location-based ticketing and closed-loop workflows. If your procurement team requires vendor questionnaires and certifications Formester doesn't hold, stay on Qualtrics.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__q">Does Formester have AI-powered analysis like Qualtrics XM Discover?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__a">Formester ships drop-off analytics, response tagging, and quiz scoring on the free plan. It does not ship the full text analytics + sentiment + theme extraction suite that Qualtrics XM Discover provides. For that, either export Formester responses to a BI tool (Power BI, Looker, Tableau) or use Qualtrics XM Discover directly.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__q">Is Qualtrics really that expensive?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__a">Public pricing isn't published, and quotes vary by seat count, response volume, and industry. Reviews on Reddit and G2 commonly report annual contracts starting in the low four figures per user, escalating with add-on products. Treat any figure as directional and confirm with Qualtrics sales. Formester's Business plan at $49/month covers 25 team seats, so per-seat cost is under $2/month at that team size.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__item">
        <summary class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__q">Who is Qualtrics&#x27; biggest competitor?</summary>
        <div class="fmstr-cmp-qua-faqs__a">For enterprise experience management, Medallia is the name most often set against Qualtrics. For general survey tooling, it is SurveyMonkey. In the self-serve form and survey space where Formester competes, shortlists usually include SurveyMonkey, Typeform, and free options like LimeSurvey and Google Forms.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
