        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "name": "Why do teams switch away from Qualtrics?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Three reasons dominate on Reddit and G2 reviews: transparent pricing (Qualtrics is enterprise-quoted, so teams can't budget without a sales call), speed to first form (Qualtrics onboarding often takes weeks with a mandatory sales demo), and per-user cost (Qualtrics charges per user, which balloons as teams grow). Formester's free plan is unlimited and self-serve, and paid tiers cap at $49/month for 25 team seats.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Is Formester really a Qualtrics replacement?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For most survey and form use cases, yes. Formester ships an AI form generator, quiz auto-scoring, drop-off analytics, custom email notifications, and native payment collection on the free plan. The genuine gaps: SOC 2 / ISO 27001 / HIPAA / FedRAMP certifications (which Qualtrics has), and specialized research tooling like IRB workflows and panel management (which Qualtrics's ResearchXM does).",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Is there a free Qualtrics alternative?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Yes. Formester's free plan gives you unlimited forms, unlimited responses, AI form generator, quiz auto-scoring, drop-off analytics, and payment collection at $0/month with no per-user seat charge. Qualtrics's free account is limited to 1 survey and 100 total responses (not per month), which is only useful for evaluation.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "What about open-source Qualtrics alternatives like LimeSurvey?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "LimeSurvey is a legitimate open-source option if you have devops capacity to self-host and don't need modern form UX. Formester is hosted (nothing to install), ships an AI generator, native payments, and a modern editor that LimeSurvey doesn't match. Choose LimeSurvey if data sovereignty is non-negotiable; choose Formester if you want a working product day one.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Which is better for students or academic research?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "For a simple class project or student survey, Formester's free plan (unlimited responses) will outperform Qualtrics's free tier (100 total responses, not per month). For thesis-level academic research that needs IRB approval and panel recruitment, Qualtrics ResearchXM remains the specialized tool of choice.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Can I export my Qualtrics surveys and responses into Formester?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Yes. Export Qualtrics responses as CSV or SPSS from the reporting panel, and export survey structure as QSF. In Formester, either paste the question list into the AI generator or rebuild in the drag-and-drop builder. Most single-survey migrations finish in 20-30 minutes.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "When is Qualtrics still the better choice?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Regulated research (healthcare, government, financial services) that requires SOC 2, HIPAA, or FedRAMP. Large panel-based studies with IRB workflows. Enterprise CX programs with location-based ticketing and closed-loop workflows. If your procurement team requires vendor questionnaires and certifications Formester doesn't hold, stay on Qualtrics.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Does Formester have AI-powered analysis like Qualtrics XM Discover?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Formester ships drop-off analytics, response tagging, and quiz scoring on the free plan. It does not ship the full text analytics + sentiment + theme extraction suite that Qualtrics XM Discover provides. For that, either export Formester responses to a BI tool (Power BI, Looker, Tableau) or use Qualtrics XM Discover directly.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "Is Qualtrics really that expensive?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "Public pricing isn't published, and quotes vary by seat count, response volume, and industry. Reddit and G2 reviews consistently mention CoreXM starting around $1,500/user/year for small teams, escalating with add-ons (ResearchXM, XM Discover, EmployeeXM). Formester's Business plan at $49/month covers 25 team seats, so per-seat cost is under $2/month at that team size.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "What do Reddit users say about Qualtrics alternatives?",
            "@type": "Question",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "text": "The r/AskStatistics thread that ranks #2 for 'qualtrics alternatives' recommends LimeSurvey (open source), SurveyMonkey (mainstream), and Google Forms (simple). Formester wasn't in that thread but sits between LimeSurvey and SurveyMonkey on price-to-feature: hosted like SurveyMonkey, unlimited free like LimeSurvey, ships AI generator that neither does.",
              "@type": "Answer"
            }
          }
        ]
